{"id":"e6b8c185a8e2ca347f714a24c6d96fb1f0ee8e3a","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"e6b8c185a8e2ca347f714a24c6d96fb1f0ee8e3a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/dedupe-link-dependencies-by-target.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/installing.deps-restorer\": patch","+\"@pnpm/installing.linking.modules-cleaner\": patch","+\"pacquet\": patch","+\"pnpm\": patch","+---","+","+With `dedupeDirectDeps`, `pnpm install` now compares `link:` dependencies by the directory they point at. A project's `link:` dependency is removed when the workspace root links the same directory under a different path. It is kept when the root's `link:` dependency has the same text but points at another directory.","+","+With `nodeLinker: hoisted` and `dedupeDirectDeps`, `pnpm install` now removes a project's `link:` dependency that the workspace root provides.","+","+With `nodeLinker: hoisted`, `pnpm install` now reports each `link:` dependency it removes."],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/tests/suite/dedupe_direct_deps.rs","lines":["@@ -840,84 +840,3 @@ fn dedupe_under_shamefully_hoist() {"," ","     drop((root, mock_instance));"," }","-","-/// `link:` payloads are stored relative to their own importer, so two","-/// importers can spell the same string while resolving to different","-/// directories. The prune's version-string dedupe fires on the pair","-/// anyway; the relink behind it is what keeps the importer pointing at","-/// its own target.","-#[test]","-fn relative_link_payloads_survive_the_dedupe_prune() {","-    let CommandTempCwd {","-        pacquet,","-        root,","-        workspace,","-        npmrc_info,","-        ..","-    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","-    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","-","-    fs::write(","-        workspace.join(\"package.json\"),","-        serde_json::json!({","-            \"name\": \"ws-root\",","-            \"version\": \"0.0.0\",","-            \"private\": true,","-            \"dependencies\": { \"x\": \"link:vendor/x\" },","-        })","-        .to_string(),","-    )","-    .expect(\"write root package.json\");","-","-    append_workspace_yaml_key(&workspace, \"packages\", \"['packages/*']\");","-    append_workspace_yaml_key(&workspace, \"dedupeDirectDeps\", true);","-","-    fs::create_dir_all(workspace.join(\"vendor/x\")).expect(\"mkdir vendor/x\");","-    fs::write(","-        workspace.join(\"vendor/x/package.json\"),","-        serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"@scope/root-x\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\" }).to_string(),","-    )","-    .expect(\"write vendor/x/package.json\");","-","-    fs::create_dir_all(workspace.join(\"packages/app/vendor/x\")).expect(\"mkdir app vendor/x\");","-    fs::write(","-        workspace.join(\"packages/app/vendor/x/package.json\"),","-        serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"@scope/app-x\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\" }).to_string(),","-    )","-    .expect(\"write app vendor/x/package.json\");","-    fs::write(","-        workspace.join(\"packages/app/package.json\"),","-        serde_json::json!({","-            \"name\": \"@scope/app\",","-            \"version\": \"1.0.0\",","-            \"dependencies\": { \"x\": \"link:vendor/x\" },","-        })","-        .to_string(),","-    )","-    .expect(\"write packages/app/package.json\");","-","-    pacquet","-        .with_arg(\"install\")","-        .assert()","-        .success();","-    // The second install is the one that prunes: only then does a","-    // current lockfile record the importer's link.","-    pacquet_at(&workspace)","-        .with_arg(\"install\")","-        .assert()","-        .success();","-","-    let app_link = workspace.join(\"packages/app/node_modules/x\");","-    let app_link_linked = is_symlink_or_junction(&app_link).expect(\"query app symlink\");","-    eprintln!(\"app_link={app_link:?} linked={app_link_linked}\");","-    assert!(app_link_linked, \"app's link must survive at {app_link:?}\");","-    let linked_manifest =","-        fs::read_to_string(app_link.join(\"package.json\")).expect(\"read the linked manifest\");","-    eprintln!(\"linked_manifest={linked_manifest}\");","-    assert!(","-        linked_manifest.contains(\"@scope/app-x\"),","-        \"app's `link:vendor/x` must resolve to its own vendor/x, not the root's\",","-    );","-","-    drop((root, mock_instance));","-}"],"additions":0,"deletions":81,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/tests/suite/main.rs","lines":["@@ -199,6 +199,7 @@ mod setting_flags;"," mod side_effects_cache;"," mod side_effects_cache_exclude;"," mod stage;","+mod stale_link_prune;"," mod stale_pin_dedupe;"," mod star_tests;"," mod stars_tests;"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/tests/suite/stale_link_prune.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,221 @@","+//! Which `link:` dependencies an install unlinks and reports as removed,","+//! under each node linker.","+","+use crate::_utils;","+","+use _utils::{append_workspace_yaml_key, assert_success, ndjson_records, pacquet_in};","+use command_extra::CommandExtra;","+use pnpm_testing_utils::{","+    bin::{AddMockedRegistry, CommandTempCwd},","+    fs::is_symlink_or_junction,","+};","+use serde_json::{Value, json};","+use std::{fs, path::Path, process::Command};","+","+const LINKERS: [&str; 2] = [\"isolated\", \"hoisted\"];","+","+fn write_json(path: &Path, value: &Value) {","+    fs::create_dir_all(path.parent().expect(\"a parent dir\")).expect(\"create the parent dir\");","+    fs::write(path, value.to_string()).expect(\"write the JSON file\");","+}","+","+fn write_root_manifest(workspace: &Path, dependencies: &Value) {","+    write_json(","+        &workspace.join(\"package.json\"),","+        &json!({ \"name\": \"ws-root\", \"private\": true, \"dependencies\": dependencies }),","+    );","+}","+","+fn install(pacquet: Command) -> Vec<Value> {","+    let output = pacquet","+        .with_args([\"install\", \"--reporter=ndjson\"])","+        .output()","+        .expect(\"run pnpm install\");","+    assert_success(&output);","+    ndjson_records(&output)","+}","+","+/// The `(project dir name, alias)` of each `pnpm:root` `removed` event.","+fn removals(records: &[Value]) -> Vec<(String, String)> {","+    records","+        .iter()","+        .filter(|record| record[\"name\"] == \"pnpm:root\")","+        .filter_map(|record| {","+            let prefix = Path::new(record[\"prefix\"].as_str()?);","+            let project = prefix","+                .file_name()?","+                .to_string_lossy()","+                .into_owned();","+            Some((project, record[\"removed\"][\"name\"].as_str()?.to_owned()))","+        })","+        .collect()","+}","+","+fn is_linked(path: &Path) -> bool {","+    is_symlink_or_junction(path).expect(\"query the link\")","+}","+","+/// Runs `scenario` in a fresh workspace per node linker, returning what","+/// it observed under each.","+fn under_each_linker<Observed>(","+    scenario: impl Fn(Command, &Path) -> Observed,","+) -> Vec<(&'static str, Observed)> {","+    LINKERS","+        .into_iter()","+        .map(|linker| {","+            let CommandTempCwd {","+                pacquet,","+                root,","+                workspace,","+                npmrc_info,","+                ..","+            } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+            let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+            append_workspace_yaml_key(&workspace, \"nodeLinker\", linker);","+            append_workspace_yaml_key(&workspace, \"packages\", \"['packages/*']\");","+            let observed = scenario(pacquet, &workspace);","+            drop((root, mock_instance));","+            (linker, observed)","+        })","+        .collect()","+}","+","+/// What a scenario saw of the link it removes.","+#[derive(Debug)]","+struct LinkRemoval {","+    linked_before: bool,","+    present_after: bool,","+    /// See [`removals`].","+    removals: Vec<(String, String)>,","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn a_removed_link_dependency_is_reported() {","+    let observed = under_each_linker(|pacquet, workspace| {","+        write_json(&workspace.join(\"lib/package.json\"), &json!({ \"name\": \"lib\" }));","+        write_root_manifest(workspace, &json!({ \"lib\": \"link:lib\" }));","+        install(pacquet);","+        let link = workspace.join(\"node_modules/lib\");","+        let linked_before = is_linked(&link);","+","+        write_root_manifest(workspace, &json!({}));","+        let records = install(pacquet_in(workspace));","+        LinkRemoval {","+            linked_before,","+            present_after: fs::symlink_metadata(&link).is_ok(),","+            removals: removals(&records),","+        }","+    });","+    dbg!(&observed);","+    for (linker, removal) in observed {","+        assert!(removal.linked_before, \"nodeLinker: {linker}\");","+        assert!(!removal.present_after, \"nodeLinker: {linker}\");","+        let aliases: Vec<_> = removal.removals","+            .into_iter()","+            .map(|(_, alias)| alias)","+            .collect();","+        assert_eq!(aliases, [\"lib\"], \"nodeLinker: {linker}\");","+    }","+}","+","+/// The root names `packages/shared` as `link:packages/shared`, the project","+/// as `link:../shared`: one target, so the root's link dedupes the","+/// project's.","+fn dedupe_a_project_link_under_another_spelling(pacquet: Command, workspace: &Path) -> LinkRemoval {","+    append_workspace_yaml_key(workspace, \"dedupeDirectDeps\", true);","+    write_json(&workspace.join(\"packages/shared/package.json\"), &json!({ \"name\": \"shared\" }));","+    write_json(","+        &workspace.join(\"packages/app/package.json\"),","+        &json!({ \"name\": \"app\", \"dependencies\": { \"shared\": \"link:../shared\" } }),","+    );","+    write_root_manifest(workspace, &json!({}));","+    install(pacquet);","+    let app_link = workspace.join(\"packages/app/node_modules/shared\");","+    let linked_before = is_linked(&app_link);","+","+    write_root_manifest(workspace, &json!({ \"shared\": \"link:packages/shared\" }));","+    let records = install(pacquet_in(workspace));","+    LinkRemoval {","+        linked_before,","+        present_after: fs::symlink_metadata(&app_link).is_ok(),","+        removals: removals(&records),","+    }","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn a_project_link_the_root_starts_providing_under_another_spelling_is_removed() {","+    let observed = under_each_linker(dedupe_a_project_link_under_another_spelling);","+    dbg!(&observed);","+    for (linker, removal) in observed {","+        assert!(removal.linked_before, \"nodeLinker: {linker}\");","+        assert!(!removal.present_after, \"nodeLinker: {linker}\");","+        assert_eq!(","+            removal.removals,","+            [(\"app\".to_owned(), \"shared\".to_owned())],","+            \"nodeLinker: {linker}\",","+        );","+    }","+}","+","+/// The lockfile still records the project's deduped link, so each later","+/// install finds it stale again, with nothing left to unlink. Hoisted only:","+/// the isolated linker reports it again (pnpm/tasks#293).","+#[test]","+fn a_deduped_link_is_reported_once() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    append_workspace_yaml_key(&workspace, \"nodeLinker\", \"hoisted\");","+    append_workspace_yaml_key(&workspace, \"packages\", \"['packages/*']\");","+    dedupe_a_project_link_under_another_spelling(pacquet, &workspace);","+","+    write_json(&workspace.join(\"other/package.json\"), &json!({ \"name\": \"other\" }));","+    write_root_manifest(","+        &workspace,","+        &json!({ \"shared\": \"link:packages/shared\", \"other\": \"link:other\" }),","+    );","+    let removals = removals(&install(pacquet_in(&workspace)));","+    assert_eq!(removals, []);","+","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}","+","+/// The root and the project both record `link:vendor/x`, each meaning its","+/// own `vendor/x`, so the root's link does not dedupe the project's.","+#[test]","+fn a_project_link_spelled_like_the_roots_to_another_dir_is_kept() {","+    let observed = under_each_linker(|pacquet, workspace| {","+        append_workspace_yaml_key(workspace, \"dedupeDirectDeps\", true);","+        write_json(&workspace.join(\"vendor/x/package.json\"), &json!({ \"name\": \"root-x\" }));","+        write_json(","+            &workspace.join(\"packages/app/vendor/x/package.json\"),","+            &json!({ \"name\": \"app-x\" }),","+        );","+        write_json(","+            &workspace.join(\"packages/app/package.json\"),","+            &json!({ \"name\": \"app\", \"dependencies\": { \"x\": \"link:vendor/x\" } }),","+        );","+        write_root_manifest(workspace, &json!({ \"x\": \"link:vendor/x\" }));","+        install(pacquet);","+        // A second install with a change to make, so it runs the prune.","+        write_json(&workspace.join(\"other/package.json\"), &json!({ \"name\": \"other\" }));","+        write_root_manifest(workspace, &json!({ \"x\": \"link:vendor/x\", \"other\": \"link:other\" }));","+        let records = install(pacquet_in(workspace));","+        let app_link = workspace.join(\"packages/app/node_modules/x\");","+        let target_name = fs::read_to_string(app_link.join(\"package.json\"))","+            .ok()","+            .and_then(|manifest| serde_json::from_str::<Value>(&manifest).ok())","+            .map(|manifest| manifest[\"name\"].clone());","+        (target_name, removals(&records))","+    });","+    dbg!(&observed);","+    for (linker, (target_name, removals)) in observed {","+        assert_eq!(target_name, Some(json!(\"app-x\")), \"nodeLinker: {linker}\");","+        assert_eq!(removals, [], \"nodeLinker: {linker}\");","+    }","+}"],"additions":221,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/deps-restorer/src/install_frozen_lockfile/hoisted.rs","lines":["@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ pub fn run_hoisted_linker<Reporter: self::Reporter>(","     let walked = walk_hoisted_graph(inputs, lockfile, skipped)?;","     forget_replaced_hoisted_locations(inputs, &walked)?;","     unlink_prior_workspace_hoists(inputs)?;","-    unlink_stale_direct_links(inputs, skipped)?;","+    unlink_stale_direct_links::<Reporter>(inputs, skipped)?;","     let (mut bins, hoisted_dependencies) =","         link_hoisted::<Reporter>(inputs, lockfile, &walked, skipped)?;","     record_hoisted_archives(inputs, &walked.graph);"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/deps-restorer/src/install_frozen_lockfile/hoisted/stale_links.rs","lines":["@@ -2,8 +2,8 @@"," //! before the linker writes the tree."," "," use super::{HoistedLinkerError, HoistedLinkerInputs, workspace_links::ALL_DEPENDENCY_GROUPS};","-use crate::SkippedSnapshots;","-use pnpm_reporter::SilentReporter;","+use crate::{SkippedSnapshots, prune_stale_modules::ReportedRemovals};","+use pnpm_reporter::Reporter;"," "," /// Runs before the linker writes the tree, so no package is imported at"," /// a path that is still a project's link.","@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ pub(super) fn unlink_prior_workspace_hoists("," "," /// Runs before the linker writes the tree, so a package that replaces a"," /// removed `link:` dependency is not imported through the old link.","-pub(super) fn unlink_stale_direct_links(","+pub(super) fn unlink_stale_direct_links<Reporter: self::Reporter>(","     inputs: &HoistedLinkerInputs<'_>,","     skipped: &SkippedSnapshots,"," ) -> Result<(), HoistedLinkerError> {","@@ -37,12 +37,9 @@ pub(super) fn unlink_stale_direct_links(","         wanted_lockfile: inputs.graph.lockfile,","         current_lockfile,","         linked: crate::LinkedDirectDeps { included_groups: &ALL_DEPENDENCY_GROUPS, skipped },","-        // Off until the dedupe compares resolved `link:` targets as the","-        // link pass does (pnpm/tasks#289).","-        dedupe_direct_deps: false,","+        dedupe_direct_deps: inputs.config.dedupe_direct_deps,","+        reported: ReportedRemovals::UnlinkedLinkDependencies,","     }","-    // `report_direct_dependency_changes` reports this linker's other","-    // removals; a `link:` removal goes unreported (pnpm/tasks#289).","-    .unlink::<SilentReporter>()","+    .unlink::<Reporter>()","     .map_err(HoistedLinkerError::PruneStaleLinks)"," }"],"additions":6,"deletions":9,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/deps-restorer/src/prune_direct_deps.rs","lines":["@@ -221,7 +221,12 @@ pub fn selected_groups(included: IncludedDependencies) -> Vec<DependencyGroup> {","     groups"," }"," ","-pub fn remove_direct_dep_link(modules_dir: &Path, name: &str) -> Result<(), PruneDirectDepsError> {","+/// Removes the `<modules_dir>/<name>` link and the bin shims of its","+/// package. Returns whether there was a link to remove.","+pub fn remove_direct_dep_link(","+    modules_dir: &Path,","+    name: &str,","+) -> Result<bool, PruneDirectDepsError> {","     let link =","         safe_join_modules_dir(modules_dir, name).map_err(PruneDirectDepsError::InvalidAlias)?;","     // For a scoped alias the join passes through `@scope/`; refuse to","@@ -230,18 +235,18 @@ pub fn remove_direct_dep_link(modules_dir: &Path, name: &str) -> Result<(), Prun","         && parent != modules_dir","         && !is_real_dir(parent)","     {","-        return Ok(());","+        return Ok(false);","     }","     // Only a symlink (junction on Windows) can be a direct-dep entry the","     // isolated linker wrote; anything else stays untouched. The probe","     // also covers \"not there at all\" — nothing to remove.","     if read_symlink_dir(&link).is_err() {","-        return Ok(());","+        return Ok(false);","     }","     remove_dep_bins(modules_dir, &link)?;","     match remove_symlink_dir(&link) {","-        Ok(()) => Ok(()),","-        Err(error) if error.kind() == io::ErrorKind::NotFound => Ok(()),","+        Ok(()) => Ok(true),","+        Err(error) if error.kind() == io::ErrorKind::NotFound => Ok(false),","         Err(error) => Err(PruneDirectDepsError::RemoveLink { path: link, error }),","     }"," }"],"additions":10,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/deps-restorer/src/prune_stale_modules.rs","lines":["@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ use crate::{","     prune_direct_deps::{","         PruneDirectDepsError, confined_modules_dir, is_real_dir, remove_direct_dep_link,","     },","-    symlink_direct_dependencies::{importer_root_dir, validate_importer_id},","+    symlink_direct_dependencies::{importer_root_dir, link_target_dir, validate_importer_id},"," };"," use pnpm_config::Config;"," use pnpm_lockfile::{","@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ use pnpm_reporter::{"," use std::{","     collections::{HashMap, HashSet},","     ffi::OsStr,","-    path::Path,","+    path::{Path, PathBuf},"," };"," "," /// Remove what a previous install materialized that the wanted lockfile","@@ -85,6 +85,7 @@ impl PruneStaleModules<'_> {","             current_lockfile: self.current_lockfile,","             linked: self.linked,","             dedupe_direct_deps: self.config.dedupe_direct_deps,","+            reported: ReportedRemovals::Every,","         }","         .unlink::<Reporter>()?;"," ","@@ -127,11 +128,34 @@ pub(crate) struct StaleDirectDepLinks<'a> {","     pub current_lockfile: &'a Lockfile,","     pub linked: LinkedDirectDeps<'a>,","     pub dedupe_direct_deps: bool,","+    pub reported: ReportedRemovals,","+}","+","+/// Which removals [`StaleDirectDepLinks::unlink`] reports.","+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]","+pub(crate) enum ReportedRemovals {","+    Every,","+    /// The `link:` dependencies whose link the pass removed. The hoisted","+    /// linker reports its other removals from","+    /// [`crate::report_direct_dependency_changes`].","+    UnlinkedLinkDependencies,","+}","+","+i